{"story_id":41060,"updated_at":"2026-10-24T02:23:29","headline_en":"Pakistani forces kill 10 people in operations across Gwadar district","headline_hi":"पाकिस्तानी बलों ने ग्वादर जिले भर में अभियानों में 10 लोगों को मार गिराया","payload_en":{"story_id":41060,"headline":"Pakistani forces kill 10 people in operations across Gwadar district","counts":{"articles":11,"independent_sources":8,"outlets":10},"has_established":false,"qualified_by":"interim","perspective_mode":"none","perspectives":{"–":["Anadolu Agency","Business Recorder","Daily Times","Dawn","Geo News","Hum News English","Latest news from Azerbaijan","Pakistan Observer","The Express Tribune","The News Pakistan"]},"framing":[],"suicide":false,"thread":41060,"parents":[],"children":[],"written_at":"2026-10-24T02:23:29","category":{"primary":["world"],"secondary":["abroad","conflicts"]},"places":[],"people":["Gwadar","Radio Pakistan","Inter-Services Public Relations","Asif Ali Zardari","Fitna","Pakistani","Staff Field Marshal Asim","Syed Asim Munir"],"narrative":{"paragraphs":[[{"text":"Pakistani forces killed at least 10 individuals in operations across Gwadar and surrounding areas, Inter-Services Public Relations said.","ids":[66817],"class":"unverified","sources":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8]}],[{"text":"Since 2021, Pakistan has experienced an increase in cross-border terrorist incidents.","ids":[66750],"class":"single","sources":[8]},{"text":"Terrorist attacks in Balochistan rose from 83 in July to 89 in August, Pakistan Institute for Conflict and Security Studies said, after an earlier figure showed an increase of seven per cent.","ids":[66880,66851],"class":"single","sources":[2,7]}],[{"text":"Radio Pakistan reported that security forces killed three terrorists while foiling an attempt to attack an unoccupied construction company camp in Gwadar.","ids":[66816],"class":"single","sources":[5]}],[{"text":"On Friday, Field Marshal Asim Munir visited Corps Headquarters in Peshawar.","ids":[66843],"class":"single","sources":[1,3]}],[{"text":"On Thursday, President Asif Ali Zardari praised security forces for the Gwadar operations.","ids":[66886],"class":"unverified","sources":[2,5,7]}],[{"text":"On 22 October, one civilian was killed during the attacks, and they were carried out by Indian-sponsored groups and Fitna al-Hindustan, ISPR said.","ids":[66752,66753,66754],"class":"single","sources":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]}],[{"text":"On 22 October, one civilian died in Gwadar district, attackers targeted locations near the Gabd Border Crossing and inside Gwadar, a civilian was killed during attacks near the Gabd border crossing, and a civilian was killed during attacks in Gwadar city, Relations said.","ids":[66747,66818,66824,66825],"class":"single","sources":[4,5,8]}],[{"text":"Security forces suffered no casualties, Relations said.","ids":[66879],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"Field Marshal Syed Asim Munir said, \"We will continue the campaign against Indian-sponsored terrorist outfits to the fullest and hit them hard wherever they are,\" and the Pakistan Army will hit India-backed terrorists hard.","ids":[66845,66749],"class":"single","sources":[1,3,4,8]}],[{"text":"India supports militant groups operating in Pakistan, India and Islamabad stated.","ids":[66846],"class":"disputed","sources":[3]}],[{"text":"New Delhi rejects accusations of sponsoring terrorist outfits in Pakistan.","ids":[66885],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"The Pakistan army described the 10 people killed as terrorists, stated that the individuals killed \"attempted to carry out terrorist activities,\" and condemned the \"coercion of a Baloch woman into this attack.\"","ids":[66844,66883,66884],"class":"single","sources":[1,3,4]}],[{"text":"Prime Minister Muhammad Shehbaz Sharif praised the security forces for the operation, PM Office said, \"The dedicated and brave officers and personnel of the security forces have foiled the nefarious designs of terrorists in Gwadar city and around the Gabd border crossing.\"","ids":[66755],"class":"single","sources":[6]}],[{"text":"Zardari expressed grief over the civilian’s death.","ids":[66887],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"The state designates Balochistan-based groups as Fitna al Hindustan.","ids":[66849],"class":"single","sources":[7]}],[{"text":"Counterterrorism operations will continue under Azm-e-Istehkam, approved by the Federal Apex Committee on the National Action Plan, Relations said.","ids":[66823],"class":"single","sources":[4]}]],"section_keys":["news","background","background","background","happened","say","say","say","say","say","say","say","say","say","explained","next"],"sources":[{"n":1,"url":"https://www.aa.com.tr/en/asia-pacific/10-terrorists-including-woman-killed-in-gwadar-pakistan-army/4098663","outlet":"Anadolu Agency","title":"10 terrorists, including woman, killed in Gwadar: Pakistan army","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true},{"n":2,"url":"https://dailytimes.com.pk/1571250/ispr-says-10-india-sponsored-terrorists-killed-in-gwadar/","outlet":"Daily Times","title":"ISPR says 10 India-sponsored terrorists killed in Gwadar","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true},{"n":3,"url":"https://news.az/news/pakistan-army-says-10-killed-in-counter-terror-operations-in-gwadar","outlet":"Latest news from Azerbaijan","title":"Pakistan army says 10 killed in counter-terror operations in Gwadar","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true},{"n":4,"url":"https://pakobserver.net/gwadar-clearance-operation-leaves-10-terrorists-dead-including-female-attacker-ispr/","outlet":"Pakistan Observer","title":"Gwadar Clearance Operation leaves 10 Terrorists Dead, including Female Attacker: ISPR","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true},{"n":5,"url":"https://tribune.com.pk/story/2636503/10-terrorists-including-woman-killed-after-foiled-attack-in-gwadar-ispr","outlet":"The Express Tribune","title":"Security forces kill 10 Indian-sponsored terrorists in Gwadar operations: ISPR","perspective":"–","re